       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, given as no more than 850 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a total-daily-dose mix-up. These are some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day, which may be what you meant if 1,700 mg was the daily total.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, I can't enter it as written. It would need to be reviewed and confirmed with pharmacy or the prescriber first."
